# Problem\r\n\r\nIn Project Selector screen, drop-down with enum values were not displaying their text equivalents. Instead it show numbers per option.\r\n\r\nRoot cause was that the enums these dropdown were displaying are registered when C# is loaded, which only happens during the game editor and NOT the earlier Project Selector screen.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\nGo with the simple approach, in the C++ code for Project Selector settings menu hardcode these values and make a note in the .cs files to keep these enum values in sync. This is straightforward and although we have duplication, alternatives were too heavy. Also, these enum values are hardly ever going to change.\r\n\r\n## Tested\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9071eb3e-bb2a-470c-a8a1-5429928c6ad3\r\n\r\n> [!NOTE]\r\n> Built on macOS `15.7.1 ` with `1.4 GHz Quad-Core Intel Core i5` processor  and `Intel Iris Plus Graphics 645 1536 MB` graphics card.\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":709269775,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MDkyNjk3NzU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:dotnet","name":"topic:dotnet","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull re